#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-CG0562 expect=violation domain=VS
# Rule:Description: Raise an error when REPNUM is in the dataset and there are multiple records for a subject for a test within the timeframe identified by the timing variables on the record, and --REPNUM is missing or not unique per subject per test per timing variables.
#note "PLAN-grouping-key-identity (noise pair, a missed finding): VISITNUM is the only Timing variable. Two SYSBP records at VISITNUM 4.9999999999994 come first, then one at 5 -- two exact-distinct timing values that render alike ('5'). Key identity is always exact (register D64h), so they are two groups; the two-record group has an empty VSREPNUM -> rows 1 and 2 fire, row 3 (a group of one) does not. Before the plan the later one-record block overwrote the shared rendered key, every row read a count of 1 and nothing fired."
#expectViolationCount 2
#expectViolationAt row=1 USUBJID=01-701-1015 VSSEQ=1
#expectViolationAt row=2 USUBJID=01-701-1015 VSSEQ=2
#library standard=sdtmig version=3-4
#library domain-variables VS USUBJID:Identifier VSTESTCD:Topic VISITNUM:Timing VSREPNUM:Qualifier DOMAIN:Identifier
dataset VS label="Vital Signs"
col STUDYID type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col VSSEQ type=Num label="Sequence Number"
col VSTESTCD type=Char label="Vital Signs Test Short Name"
col VISITNUM type=Num label="Visit Number"
col VSREPNUM type=Char label="Repetition Number"
---
CDISCPILOT01 | VS | 01-701-1015 | 1 | SYSBP | 4.9999999999994 |
CDISCPILOT01 | VS | 01-701-1015 | 2 | SYSBP | 4.9999999999994 |
CDISCPILOT01 | VS | 01-701-1015 | 3 | SYSBP | 5 |
---
